  "id": "body-dysmorphic-disorder",
  "term": "body dysmorphic disorder",
  "definition": "Body dysmorphic disorder is a mental health condition in which a person has distressing and often strongly held beliefs about flaws in their appearance, along with significant impairment. It often begins in childhood or adolescence, is common in young people, and can be long-lasting and severe if untreated.",
